FINAL ANSWER:
**Reviewer: Graham Campbell** (<email redacted>). He wrote about 86% of the current lines in `src/Parser/`. **Priscila Duarte** (<email redacted>) should review changes to `Comments.php` or `Interpolator.php`, because she wrote all of both files.

A plain `git blame` gives the wrong answer here. It credits 791 of 912 lines to Marta Kowalczyk, but her only change was commit `45259fd`, which converted indentation to tabs in all 9 files. StyleCI commit `73c5c0f` also gets 4 lines, all `(string) $x` → `(string)$x` spacing. I re-ran the blame ignoring whitespace (`-w`), following moved and copied lines (`-M -C`), and skipping those two commits with `--ignore-rev`. Author names are combined using `.mailmap`.

Current lines by original author:

| Author | Lines |
|---|---|
| Graham Campbell | 782 |
| Priscila Duarte | 118 |
| Vance Lucas | 10 (all in `Lines.php`) |
| Jonas Staudenmeir | 1 |
| JT Smith | 1 |

By file:
- **Graham:** `EntryParser.php` (363 lines), `Lines.php` (125 of 136), `Value.php`, `Entry.php`, `Lexer.php`, `Parser.php`, `ParserInterface.php`.
- **Priscila:** `Comments.php` (56 lines), `Interpolator.php` (62 lines).

So the right reviewer depends on which file the change touches. To recheck one file:
```
git blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 45259fd --ignore-rev 73c5c0f src/Parser/<file>.php
```

One suggestion: add both commit hashes to a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file and run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`. After that, a normal blame (and GitHub's blame view) will skip the formatting commits automatically.

